            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-md);">
                <div class="card-title">📊 Descent Progress</div>
                <div class="stats-row" id="gd-stats"></div>
                <canvas id="gd-loss-canvas" width="400" height="200" style="width:100%;margin-top:var(--space-md);"></canvas>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Chain Rule -->
        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-calc-chain">
          <div class="instruction-box">
            <span class="instruction-icon">🔗</span>
            The chain rule decomposes derivatives of composite functions. See how gradients flow backward through a computation graph.
          </div>
          <div class="grid-2">
            <div class="canvas-container">
              <canvas id="chain-canvas" width="560" height="400"></canvas>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-md);">
                <div class="card-title">🔗 Chain Rule Formula</div>
                <div class="math-block">
                  If y = f(g(x)), then dy/dx = f'(g(x)) · g'(x)
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="card">
                <div class="card-title">🧠 Backprop Intuition</div>
                <div class="controls-panel" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-sm);">
                  <div class="control-group">
                    <span class="control-label">x =</span>
                    <input type="range" id="chain-x" min="-3" max="3" step="0.1" value="2" />
                    <span class="control-value" id="chain-x-val">2.0</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div id="chain-results" style="font-family:var(--font-code);font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:2;"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ========== REGRESSION (Week 7-8) ========== -->
      <section class="section" id="section-regression">
        <div class="section-header">
          <div class="section-week">Week 7 – 8</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Regression</h2>
          <p class="section-description">Linear, Polynomial, Ridge & Lasso — predicting continuous values and understanding regularization.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tabs" id="reg-tabs">
          <button class="tab active" data-tab="reg-linear">Linear Regression</button>
          <button class="tab" data-tab="reg-poly">Polynomial</button>
          <button class="tab" data-tab="reg-ridge">Ridge / Lasso</button>
        </div>

        <!-- Linear Regression -->
        <div class="tab-content active" id="tab-reg-linear">
          <div class="instruction-box">
            <span class="instruction-icon">📍</span>
            Click on the canvas to add data points. The best-fit line updates automatically.
          </div>
          <div class="controls-panel">
            <button class="btn btn-accent" id="lr-sample">📊 Sample Data</button>
            <button class="btn btn-danger" id="lr-clear">🗑 Clear All</button>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-2">
            <div class="canvas-container">
              <canvas id="linreg-canvas" width="500" height="400"></canvas>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-md);">
                <div class="card-title">📐 Best Fit Line</div>
                <div class="math-block" id="lr-equation">y = mx + b</div>
                <div class="stats-row" id="lr-stats"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="card">
                <div class="card-title">📝 How it works</div>
                <div class="math-block">
                  minimize Σ(yᵢ - (mx + b))²
                </div>
                <p style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:var(--space-sm);">
                  Linear regression finds the line that minimizes the sum of squared residuals (MSE). 
                  The slope m and intercept b are computed using the normal equation.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Polynomial Regression -->
        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-reg-poly">
          <div class="instruction-box">
            <span class="instruction-icon">🔮</span>
            Click to add points, then adjust the degree slider to see overfitting vs underfitting.
          </div>
          <div class="controls-panel">
            <div class="control-group">
              <span class="control-label">Degree</span>
              <input type="range" id="poly-degree" min="1" max="10" value="2" />
              <span class="control-value" id="poly-degree-val">2</span>
            </div>
            <button class="btn btn-accent" id="poly-sample">📊 Sample Data</button>
            <button class="btn btn-danger" id="poly-clear">🗑 Clear</button>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-2">
            <div class="canvas-container">
              <canvas id="polyreg-canvas" width="500" height="400"></canvas>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-md);">
                <div class="card-title">📊 Model Fit</div>
                <div class="stats-row" id="poly-stats"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="card">
                <div class="card-title">⚖️ Bias vs Variance</div>
                <div class="legend">
                  <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:#f59e0b;"></div> Low degree = High bias (underfitting)</div>
                  <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:#f43f5e;"></div> High degree = High variance (overfitting)</div>
                  <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:#10b981;"></div> Just right = Good generalization</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Ridge / Lasso -->
        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-reg-ridge">
          <div class="instruction-box">
            <span class="instruction-icon">🎛️</span>
            Adjust the regularization strength (α) to see how Ridge and Lasso shrink coefficients differently.
          </div>
          <div class="controls-panel">
            <div class="control-group">
              <span class="control-label">α (lambda)</span>
              <input type="range" id="reg-alpha" min="0" max="5" step="0.05" value="0" />
              <span class="control-value" id="reg-alpha-val">0.00</span>
            </div>
            <div class="control-group">
              <span class="control-label">Poly Degree</span>
              <input type="range" id="reg-degree" min="2" max="8" value="5" />
              <span class="control-value" id="reg-degree-val">5</span>
            </div>
            <button class="btn btn-accent" id="reg-new-data">🔄 New Data</button>
          </div>
          <div class="comparison-grid">
            <div>
              <div class="comparison-title">Ridge (L2)</div>
              <div class="canvas-container">
                <canvas id="ridge-canvas" width="400" height="300"></canvas>
              </div>
              <div class="stats-row" id="ridge-stats" style="margin-top:var(--space-sm);"></div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="comparison-title">Lasso (L1)</div>
              <div class="canvas-container">
                <canvas id="lasso-canvas" width="400" height="300"></canvas>
              </div>
              <div class="stats-row" id="lasso-stats" style="margin-top:var(--space-sm);"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card" style="margin-top:var(--space-lg);">
            <div class="card-title">📊 Coefficient Comparison</div>
            <canvas id="coeff-canvas" width="800" height="250" style="width:100%;"></canvas>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ========== CLASSIFICATION (Week 7-8) ========== -->
      <section class="section" id="section-classification">
        <div class="section-header">
          <div class="section-week">Week 7 – 8</div>
          <h2 class="section-title">Classification</h2>
          <p class="section-description">Logistic Regression & K-Nearest Neighbors — drawing decision boundaries to classify data.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="tabs" id="class-tabs">
          <button class="tab active" data-tab="cls-logistic">Logistic Regression</button>
          <button class="tab" data-tab="cls-knn">K-Nearest Neighbors</button>
          <button class="tab" data-tab="cls-compare">Compare</button>
        </div>

        <!-- Logistic Regression -->
        <div class="tab-content active" id="tab-cls-logistic">
          <div class="instruction-box">
            <span class="instruction-icon">🎯</span>
            Click to add Class 0 (cyan) or Class 1 (magenta) points. Toggle with the button. The decision boundary updates live.
          </div>
          <div class="controls-panel">
            <button class="btn btn-accent" id="log-class-toggle">Adding: Class 0 🔵</button>
            <button class="btn btn-accent" id="log-sample">📊 Sample Data</button>
            <button class="btn btn-danger" id="log-clear">🗑 Clear</button>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-2">
            <div class="canvas-container">
              <canvas id="logistic-canvas" width="500" height="400"></canvas>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-md);">
                <div class="card-title">📐 Model</div>
                <div class="math-block">
                  P(y=1|x) = σ(w·x + b) = 1 / (1 + e^(-(w·x + b)))
                </div>
                <div class="stats-row" id="log-stats"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="card">
                <div class="card-title">📊 Sigmoid Function</div>
                <canvas id="sigmoid-canvas" width="400" height="180" style="width:100%;"></canvas>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- KNN -->
        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-cls-knn">
          <div class="instruction-box">
            <span class="instruction-icon">👥</span>
            Click to add points of different classes. Adjust K to see how the decision boundary changes.
          </div>
          <div class="controls-panel">
            <div class="control-group">
              <span class="control-label">K =</span>
              <input type="range" id="knn-k" min="1" max="15" value="3" />
              <span class="control-value" id="knn-k-val">3</span>
            </div>
            <button class="btn btn-accent" id="knn-class-toggle">Adding: Class 0 🔵</button>
            <button class="btn btn-accent" id="knn-sample">📊 Sample Data</button>
            <button class="btn btn-danger" id="knn-clear">🗑 Clear</button>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-2">
            <div class="canvas-container">
              <canvas id="knn-canvas" width="500" height="400"></canvas>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-md);">
                <div class="card-title">📊 Metrics</div>
                <div class="stats-row" id="knn-stats"></div>
              </div>
              <div class="card">
                <div class="card-title">🔢 Confusion Matrix</div>
                <div class="confusion-matrix" id="knn-cm">
                  <div class="cm-cell cm-header"></div>
                  <div class="cm-cell cm-header">Pred 0</div>
                  <div class="cm-cell cm-header">Pred 1</div>
                  <div class="cm-cell cm-header">Act 0</div>
                  <div class="cm-cell cm-tn" id="cm-tn">0</div>
                  <div class="cm-cell cm-fp" id="cm-fp">0</div>
                  <div class="cm-cell cm-header">Act 1</div>
                  <div class="cm-cell cm-fn" id="cm-fn">0</div>
                  <div class="cm-cell cm-tp" id="cm-tp">0</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Compare -->
        <div class="tab-content" id="tab-cls-compare">
          <div class="instruction-box">
            <span class="instruction-icon">⚔️</span>
            Side-by-side comparison of Logistic Regression vs KNN on the same dataset.
          </div>
          <div class="controls-panel">
            <div class="control-group">
              <span class="control-label">K (for KNN)</span>
              <input type="range" id="cmp-k" min="1" max="15" value="5" />
              <span class="control-value" id="cmp-k-val">5</span>
            </div>
            <div class="control-group">
              <span class="control-label">Dataset</span>
              <select id="cmp-dataset">
                <option value="linear">Linearly Separable</option>
                <option value="circles">Concentric Circles</option>
                <option value="moons">Moons</option>
                <option value="xor">XOR</option>
              </select>
            </div>
            <button class="btn btn-accent" id="cmp-generate">🔄 Generate</button>
          </div>
          <div class="comparison-grid">
            <div>
              <div class="comparison-title">Logistic Regression</div>
              <div class="canvas-container">
                <canvas id="cmp-logistic-canvas" width="400" height="400"></canvas>
              </div>
              <div class="stats-row" id="cmp-log-stats" style="margin-top:var(--space-sm);"></div>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="comparison-title">KNN (K = <span id="cmp-k-display">5</span>)</div>
              <div class="canvas-container">
                <canvas id="cmp-knn-canvas" width="400" height="400"></canvas>
              </div>
              <div class="stats-row" id="cmp-knn-stats" style="margin-top:var(--space-sm);"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </main>
  </div>

  <!-- CDN Libraries -->
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.0/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>

  <!-- App Modules -->
  <script src="js/app.js"></script>
  <script src="js/python-basics.js"></script>
  <script src="js/linear-algebra.js"></script>
  <script src="js/calculus.js"></script>
  <script src="js/regression.js"></script>
  <script src="js/classification.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
